    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A product can come with a word clue. Ankit's age times Nikita's age is 240. Twice Nikita's age is four more than Ankit's.\n\nLet Nikita be n. Then Ankit is 2n − 4.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Multiply the ages:\nn(2n − 4) = 240.\n\nDivide the resulting equation by 2:\nn² − 2n − 120 = 0\n(n − 12)(n + 10) = 0.\n\nSo n = 12 or −10. Reject −10 as a present age. Ankit is 2 × 12 − 4 = 20. Check: 12 × 20 = 240 and 2 × 12 = 20 + 4.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
