    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A sum and product can also reveal the age gap. Suppose ages add to 29 and multiply to 198.\n\nThe factor pair 11 and 18 works: 11 + 18 = 29 and 11 × 18 = 198.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_6_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_6_step": {
      "id": "teach_6_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Their gap is 18 − 11 = 7.\n\nAnother way is:\n(x − y)² = (x + y)² − 4xy\n= 29² − 4 × 198\n= 49.\n\nThe age gap is the non-negative square root of 49, which is 7. Check the chosen ages against both clues.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_6"
        }
      ]
    },
